# Goal + Architect GENERAL-PURPOSE coding agent (drives = REAL tools). For each Goal
# attempt, ARCHITECT designs a team for THIS task -- it picks the best shape (Codegen for
# trying parallel implementations, or Pipeline implement -> test -> review) AND writes the
# member roles -- staffs it with CLAUDE CODE agents (full file/shell tools), and runs it.
# Goal's checker (also Claude Code) VERIFIES the acceptance condition by ACTUALLY running
# it, and re-attempts (Architect re-designs) until met.
#
# vs Jet Verified Coder (Goal+Flow): there YOU get a dataflow DAG; here the team SHAPE is
# chosen per task -- good when you don't know the best structure up front. Both genuinely
# write + run code on drives.
#
# SLOW + uses your Claude Code (many calls/round). Needs claude-code-acp.
#   jet acp-serve acp_architect_coder_demo::ArchitectCoder::handle examples/acp_architect_coder_demo.jet
# Try: "Add an is_prime(n) function to primes.py and prove it works on the first 10 primes."
module acp_architect_coder_demo
  agent ArchitectCoder
    runner Goal(accept: "the requested code or change is implemented in real files AND a SHOWN real command or test run confirms it works -- the expected behavior must appear in actual terminal output, not a described or simulated result",
                via: {name: :Architect},
                surface: true,
                max_rounds: 3,
                drives: "claude-code-acp")
    ask handle(task)
  end
end
